  "$comment": "Noun key -> OpenMoji glyph. The KEY is what an author writes in a spec ('cat'); the ANNOTATION is OpenMoji's own name for the glyph, which build_pictograms.js resolves to a hexcode against openmoji.json. Never hand-write a hexcode here: an annotation is checkable against the upstream metadata, a hexcode is a magic number. Every key is a lowercase English single word or snake_case compound. The set is deliberately small and early-years: it is the nouns a K-5 English/Urdu/Maths lesson actually counts, names, sounds out or spells, taken from the ICT K-5 and Punjab 1-5 segmentations (see the option-space study for the derivation).",
